\documentclass{article}
\title{Register Pressure in Unrolled Loop Nests}
\author{T. Bergmann}
\date{March 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Cost Model}
Our instruction scheduler estimates the live range of every temporary value.
For a square tile of side n the pressure grows like x^2 + y^2$ across the unrolled body,
so we stop unrolling once the estimate exceeds the physical register count.
This simple heuristic spills noticeably fewer temporaries than the default strategy.
\end{document}

